The cube \( C \) has **side length 1**.

An **inscribed sphere** \( O_1 \) is one that just fits inside the cube, touching the centers of all six faces. The diameter of the sphere is equal to the side of the cube.

So,

\[
\text{Diameter of } O_1 = 1 \implies \text{Radius of } O_1 = \frac{1}{2}
\]

The center of \( O_1 \) is at the center of the cube: coordinates \((0.5, 0.5, 0.5)\) if we place the cube with one corner at \((0,0,0)\) and the opposite at \((1,1,1)\).

